    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0064" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/67<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >7/24</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-25T11:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>103. Your telegram No. 84, May 23, noon.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d60-f1"/> Saw the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="70" xml:id="d60-f2"/> at 7:30 last night.
                    He said he had been favoring something of the sort and would see the
                        President<anchor n="71" xml:id="d60-f3"/> today and try to give a definite
                    answer by night. I saw the President at dinner last night and prepared him for
                    today’s conference with the Minister. Confident of acceptance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
